			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a3b095ec-6250-4f77-b486-b2c2bf78639f")
	)
	(text_box "A 50ms soft start is configured with the SS pin to keep the inrush current below 2mA while charging C3.\n\nThe voltage divider on the EN pin is set in a way that the device turns on above 6.6V and turns off below 5.6V.\n\nThe output is set to 2.7V because that's the minimum for the CO2 sensor. Without the CO2 sensor, we could go as low as 2.0V, which is the minimum for the analog circuitry in MSP430."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 210.82 48.26 0)
		(size 55.88 26.67)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c665c27e-e8d5-462a-b1f2-114f8914f0f8")
	)
	(text_box "This transistor needs to sink 260mA for 0.833ms, and 85 mA on average.\n\nEven though the bus is only 22.5V maximum, it should withstand 60V so the potential voltage spikes on the bus don't damage it.\n\nThe microcontroller's logic level (currently set to 2.5V) should fully turn it on with low enough drain-source resistance that it doesn't overheat.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 83.82 118.11 0)
		(size 34.29 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e6314d05-7d12-4a6b-8b3b-6ef6e3b6c624")
	)
